  "uses_raw": true,
  "prompt": "How many of store BE-14's order lines are left in each month of 2024 once resent copies are removed? These tables may hold errors. Some of store BE-14's order lines were resent under a new order_line_id: two lines are copies of one order line when order_id, product_id, quantity and unit_price_eur all match. Keep the copy with the lowest order_line_id. The month is the first day of the month of the order's order_ts as stored, and 2024 means order_ts, as stored, from 1 January 2024 up to but not including 1 January 2025. Return three columns, in this order: order_month, n_stored (the lines as stored) and n_kept (the lines once copies are removed). Return one row for each month with BE-14 lines. Any row order is fine.",
  "output_contract": {
    "columns": [
      {
        "name": "order_month",
        "type_class": "temporal"
      },
      {
        "name": "n_stored",
        "type_class": "numeric"
